    "title": "pandas.Index.hasnans — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1386.gcb2086a1a4 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Index.hasnans#\n\n- Index.hasnans[source]#\n- Return True if there are any NaNs. Enables various performance speedups. \n  - Returns:\n    - bool\n See also \n  - `Index.isna`\n  - Detect missing values.\n  - `Index.dropna`\n  - Return Index without NA/NaN values.\n  - `Index.fillna`\n  - Fill NA/NaN values with the specified value.\n Examples >>> s = pd.Series([1, 2, 3], index=[\"a\", \"b\", None]) >>> s a 1 b 2 None 3 dtype: int64 >>> s.index.hasnans True",
